    "note": [
      "Ladder data, not tournament results. Ladder metagames reward Pokemon that are",
      "forgiving and fast to pilot, which is not the same thing as strong.",
      "",
      "Only 93 of the 208 legal species appear. The site lists nothing below roughly 1%",
      "usage, so the tail is censored rather than absent: a species missing here is known",
      "to be under ~1%, but the 115 of them cannot be ranked against each other.",
      "",
      "Corroborated against an independent top-20 from pikalytics.com retrieved the same",
      "day, which shares 17 of 20 entries; the three that differ (Swampert, Metagross,",
      "Floette-Eternal against Tyranitar, Milotic, Delphox) all appear just outside the",
      "other list's top 20. That is agreement about a real metagame, not proof of either",
      "site's precision.",
      "",
      "Transcribed from the rendered page in a single pass and not independently",
      "reconciled row by row. Treat individual percentages as approximate; the rank",
      "order is what the correlation uses and it is internally consistent (usage",
      "descends within every tier).",
      "",
      "`usage` is the share of teams carrying the Pokemon. `winRate` is the share of",
      "games won by teams carrying it. The correlation script reports against both,",
      "but they are NOT two independent checks: they rank-correlate at 0.683, and",
      "winRate is compressed toward 50% for heavily-used Pokemon (corr of usage with",
      "|winRate - 50| is -0.438). Something on a quarter of all teams is largely",
      "playing itself and cannot post an extreme win rate, so most of the win-rate",
      "variance sits in the rare tail where each Pokemon has the fewest games.",
      "Treat agreement across the two columns as one result, not two, and do not",
      "tune a weight on either."
    ]
  },
